# This repo lives inside a live Factorio mods directory, so the default is to
# ignore everything the game or another author put here and track only the mods
# developed in this repo.

# Downloaded mods — other authors' work, and huge.
*.zip

# Game-managed. Editing or restoring these from git breaks the install.
mod-list.json
mod-settings.dat
mod-settings.json

# Folder classes below follow CLAUDE.md -> Folder classes. Being listed here means
# "not a repo deliverable" — it does NOT mean "do not touch". Two of these classes are
# edited routinely; only Frozen vendor and Reference are hands-off, and those are the
# ones that also need a deny rule in .claude/settings.json.

# Reference — extracted mods kept for study. Machine-local; a fresh clone won't have it.
/exemples/

# Frozen vendor — other authors' unpacked mods, present only so the game loads them.
# Each clone adds its own here, since only *.zip is covered automatically. Every entry
# here also needs Edit + Write deny rules in .claude/settings.json.
/robotworld-continued_2.1.0/
/VoidChestInstant_2.8.0/
/whats_a_spoilage/

# Local mod — ours, but deliberately untracked: it retunes other authors' prototypes for
# one save and is never published, so it is not a repo deliverable.
/realk-tweaks/

# Machine-specific paths, git identity and tool versions. CLAUDE.md, .claude/
# and .ai-support/ are tracked; this is the deliberate local-only escape hatch.
# CLAUDE.local.md.example is tracked as its template.
CLAUDE.local.md

# Headless --dump-data leftovers.
data-raw-dump.json
*.log

# CC0 texture/HDRI downloads (Poly Haven). Re-fetchable by slug via the
# factorio-graphics skill's scripts/polyhaven.py, so the slug in a generator
# script is the tracked source; the binaries stay out of git.
/assets/third-party/

# Blender autosaves. The .blend files under assets/ are tracked deliberately;
# these rolling backups are noise.
*.blend1
*.blend2

# Python bytecode from the asset render scripts under assets/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Nearest-neighbour blowups written by make_thumbnail.py --preview. Judging aids
# for a 144px image, regenerable in a second; the 512px master beside them is tracked.
/assets/*/thumbnail/preview-*.png

# Windows / editor noise.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp
*~

# Third-party reference screenshots dropped into any mod's .ai-support stay
# local; the design docs beside them remain tracked.
*/.ai-support/*.jpg
*/.ai-support/*.png

# Local Claude Code settings. Holds secrets (API tokens read by MCP servers),
# so it must never be committed — .claude/ is otherwise tracked.
/.claude/settings.local.json
